          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em sheafification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            universally turns
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
          %p
            It is characterized as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : PSh(C) \to Sh(C)
            to the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C) \hookrightarrow PSh(C)
            of sheaves into all presheaves, exhibiting this as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
          %p
            Therefore sheafification is a special case of a very general phenomenon of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localizations
            of categories. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            for more.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            in the sense of:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            equipped with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j : C \to PSh(C)
          %p
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i :  Sh_J(C) \hookrightarrow PSh(C)
          %p
            for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            on those presheaves that are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
          %h3#existence Existence
          #ExistenceOfLeftAdjoint.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The inclusion of sheaves into presheaves admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              or reflective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv i) : Sh_J(C) \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    PSh(C)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This follows by general properties discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              at a set of morphisms satisfying a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            %p
              Recall from the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_J(C)
              is by definition the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local objects
              with respect to the morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi i
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W =
                    \\left\{
                    S(\{U_i\}) := \lim_\to\left(
                    \\coprod_{i,j} j(U_i) \times_{j(U)} j(U_j) \stackrel{\to}{\to} \coprod_i j(U_i) \right) \to j(U)
                    |
                    \\;\;
                    \\{U_i \to U\}_{i \in I} \in J
                    \\right\}
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              inclusions for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              families of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              of the two injection maps, as indicated. This is spelled out in more detail at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              and at
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
            %p Now we invoke the following results:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/reflective+sub-(infinity%2C1)-category#LocalizationProposition"} localization proposition
                  says that every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
                  on the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local objects
                  for a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  of morphisms is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                  at these morphisms;
              %li
                %p
                  By
                  %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory#CharacterizationByLocalization"} Gabriel-Zisman's theorem
                  every reflective subcategory is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                  at the collection of morphisms inverted by the left adjoint (which by the localization proposition is the saturation of the original set of morphisms).
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  satisfies the axioms of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
                  then, by the discussion there, this localization is equivalently given by the category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)[W^{-1}]
                  whose objects are those of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
                  and whose morphisms are given by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi W
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi lim
                                %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi w
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                              %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mi PSh
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)[W^{-1}](X,A) \simeq {\lim_{\to}}_{\hat X  \stackrel{w \in W}{\to} X} PSh_C(\hat X,A)
            %p
              Notice that an object is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              with respect to the above set of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              precisely if it is local with respect to the set of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
              (in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(PSh(C))
              ) of such morphims (since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_C(-,A)
              sends colimits in the first argument to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphisms
              is an isomorphism).
            %p
              Let hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              be the completion of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              under forming small colimits in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Arr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(PSh(C))
            %p
              We claim that the morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              form a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to j(U)
              and every covering family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
              there is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi s
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; S(\{U_i\})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{s}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; j(U)
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in W \subset \bar W
              to deduce the stability conditions for all morphisms in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              the pullback of a colimit is a colimit of pullbacks.)
            %p
              Similarly, to see that we can find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              we use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
              to decompose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mo
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \simeq {\lim_{\to}_j} K_j
              and then use
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
              to deduce that we are looking at a diagram of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi r
                            %msup
                              %mi s
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi K
                              %mi r
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi s
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi r
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi K
                              %mi r
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    {\lim_{\to}}_r s^* K_r &amp;\to&amp; S(\{U_i\})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{s}}
                    \\\
                    {\lim_\to}_r j(K_r) &amp;\to&amp; j(U)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              is closed under colimits, it is hence sufficient that we show the stability condition for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any representable. So we need to fill diagrams of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi s
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; S(\{U_i\})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{s}}
                    \\\
                    j(K) &amp;\to&amp; j(U)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              For this now use the single condition on a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
              a covering family in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
              we can find a covering family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{K_j \to K\}
              such that every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_j \to K
              factors through one of the
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \to U
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieves
              factor, and we have a commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi K
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S(\{K_j\}) &amp;\to&amp; S(\{U_i\})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    j(K) &amp;\to&amp; j(U)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              satisfies the first condition at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorization system
            %p
              The second condition at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
              demands that if two composites of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{\to}{\to} S(\{U_i\}) \to j(U)
            %p
              are equal in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              such that the two composites
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y \to X \stackrel{\to}{\to} S(\{U_i\})
            %p
              are equal. But the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              inclusions are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              on
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
              and using
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
              and the pasting law for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullbacks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo ,
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    {\lim_\to}_k X_k &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \downarrow
                    \\\
                    {\lim_\to}_k S(U_{k,i}) &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    {\lim_\to}_k j(U_k) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; j(U)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              by applying the above on each component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              of the colimit.
            %p
              This gives us the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : PSh(C) \to Sh_J(C)
              as described at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_J(C)
              is equivalently given by the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)[W^{-1}]
              with the same objects as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-sets
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi w
                            %mo ∈
                            %mover
                              %mi W
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh(C)[W^{-1}](X,A)
                    \\simeq
                    {\lim_\to}_{\{\hat X \stackrel{w \in \hat W}{\to} X\}}
                    PSh_C(\hat X,A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              So we have that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(C)
              a presheaf and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Sh_J(C)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_C(L(X),A)
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi w
                            %mo ∈
                            %mover
                              %mi W
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh_C(L(X), A) \simeq
                    {\lim_{\to}}_{\hat X \stackrel{w \in \bar W}{\to} X} PSh_C(\hat X,A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              But if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a sheaf, it is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi w
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_C(\hat X \stackrel{w}{\to} X, A)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in \bar W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo =
                    %mi Id
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w = Id : X \to X
              therefore we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \simeq
                    PSh_C(X,A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This demonstrates the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv i)
          %h3#construction Construction
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(C)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
              %strong sheafification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(X)
              is the presheaf given on any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mover
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi w
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(X) : U \mapsto {\lim_\to}_{\{\hat U \stackrel{w}{\to} j(U)\}} PSh_C(\hat U, X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              on the right is over all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in \bar W
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(X)(U) \simeq PSh_C(j(U), L(X))
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "#ExistenceOfLeftAdjoint"} above proposition
              this is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \simeq Sh_C(L(j(U)), L(X))
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the proof of the above proposition, using the formulas discussed at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mover
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi w
                            %mo ∈
                            %mover
                              %mi W
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \simeq {\lim_\to}_{\{ \hat U \stackrel{w \in \bar W}{\to} j(U)\}} PSh_C(\hat U, X)
                    \\,.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
            %p
              By the definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat U \to j(U)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
              are colimits of diagrams of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi K
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi K
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat U \simeq
                    {\lim_\to}_{\{K \to U\}} S(\{K_i\}) \to {\lim_\to}_{\{K \to U\}} j(K)
                    \\,.
            %p This means (…) that the above colimit may be computed as two consecutive colimits of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\lim_{\to}}_{\{S(\{U_i\}) \to j(U)\}} PSh_C(S(\{U_i\}), X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              One such application is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plus+construction"} plus construction
            %p
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\}) \to X
              out of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              into any presheaf is in components precisely a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matching+family"} matching family
              of the presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
            %p
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Use that the sieve is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S(\{U_i\}) \to \coprod_i j(U_i) \stackrel{\to}{\to}
                    \\coprod_{i,j} j(U_i) \times_{j(U)} j(U_j)
            %p
              and that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_C(-,X)
              sends
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv i)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              has as components natural morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to L X
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
              these morphisms are mapped to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphisms
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo :
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : PSh(C) \to Sh(C)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphisms
            %p
              So every presheaf is related by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
              to its sheafification.
          %h2#for_sheaves_with_values_in_categories_other_than_
            For sheaves with values in categories other than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            For presheaves with values in categories other than
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#with_values_in_models_for_finitelimit_theories With values in models for finite-limit theories
          %p
            Consider a type of structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            defined in terms of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theory"} essentially algebraic theory
            finite limits (such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+algebraic+theory"} models
            are preserved by both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct images
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse images
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv i) : Sh_J(C) \to PSh(C)
            directly induces an adjunction between
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-models-in-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %h3#using_the_ipcproperty Using the IPC-property
          %p
            If a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            satisfies the following assumptions, sheafification of presheaves in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, A]
            exists and is constructed analogously as for
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              admits small
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              admits small
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
            %li
              small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered colimits
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              are exact;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              satisfies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/IPC-property"} IPC-property
              \.
          %p This is true for instance for
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                of sets;
            %li
              %p
                the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                of groups;
            %li
              %p
                the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Alg
                of
                = succeed "-algebras;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %li
              %p
                the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(R)
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} modules
          %p
            (but all of these are also
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong> sheafification
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plus-construction+on+presheaves"} plus-construction on presheaves
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheafification"} (∞,1)-sheafification
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The description of sheafification in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphisms
            is in section 16.3 (for
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %ul
            %li
              Kashiwara–Schapira,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
          %p
            The description in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+monomorphism"} dense monomorphisms
            using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
            is in section V.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"} Saunders Mac Lane
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p
            Sheafification is shown to be instance of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+enriched+in+a+bicategory"} bicategory-enriched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy completion
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renato+Betti"} Renato Betti
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aurelio+Carboni"} Aurelio Carboni
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cauchy-completion and the associated sheaf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1982__23_3_243_0.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renato+Betti"} Renato Betti
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Walters"} Robert Walters
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The symmetry of the Cauchy-completion of a category
          %p Extension of sheafification of presheaves with values in other categories has been advanced in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Heller"}> Alex Heller
                , K. A. Rowe,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the category of sheaves
            %li
              %p
                Barr, Grillet, and Van Osdol,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Exact categories and categories of sheaves
            %li
              %p
                Friedrich Ulmer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the existence and exactness of the associated sheaf functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"}> Alexander Rosenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Almost quotient categories, sheaves and localizations
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#QuirinTabareau16
              Kevin Quirin, Nicolas Tabareau,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lawvere-Tierney sheafification in Homotopy Type Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://jfr.unibo.it/article/view/6232"} web
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/sheaf+theory"} sheaf theory
